    "turn_text": "the success I see is of anything. It's, of course, the mineral exploration and the oil exploration has been successful and we have not developed. But we know the potential there. There is a lot of people in America to understand it. Above the Arctic Circle, on the coastal plain, there's over 40 billion barrels in existence a day of fossil fuels. And to some people that's not good, but to the nations and whole, that's very good. It's not the fuel that we're pumping now. We drill through three different layers of oil to get to what we call the premium oil, a high quality oil. But all above that are different velocities of the oil that we learn more. We'll be able to extract that for this nation.",
