  {
    "episode_id": 45963,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45963.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Education, education, education, education. And talking to people, informing, as I said, people in an era, TV shows about something besides the ones that show now, which are mostly all nonsense, but scientific shows. I believe that's going to be the real challenge. I would hate to say that if we really want to see fast progress, we'll have a conflict. We watched what happened in the Arctic. When we had World War II, we built a highway, the Canada Highway, in 11 months, because we were under stress. When we were not under stress, you don't do anything. I'm not advocating for a conflict, but I'm saying you want to see somebody really pay attention to the Arctic. Just have something going up there that really gets everybody's attention on Lord 48.",
