    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45963.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "I live above the Arctic Circle. I'm about 400 miles from the so-called Arctic Ocean. But I've spent quite a bit of time in my career not only visiting most of those villages. I've seen whales taken, which is very interesting. I happen to think that any of the people are some of the smartest people in the world. And they have a great organization up there, the Arctic Regional Corporation. And it's just a lot of things have happened to the Arctic. Personally, I live in the coldest place in the state. In 1964, it was 79 below zero. One day January 14th, and it warmed up to 60 below for 60 straight days, two full months. That's the coldest I've ever been.",
